# The builder gets the whole checkout, .git included: the go command reads the
# version and commit from it and stamps them into the binary (see
# internal/buildinfo). Only the build stage sees any of it; the image gets the
# binary alone.
#
# Never list a tracked file here. git in the builder would see it as deleted
# and mark every build as modified (+dirty). What is listed is what .gitignore
# keeps out of the repository, so keep the two in step: secrets and databases
# must not reach the builder, the rest is bulk. A file only your global git
# excludes ignore still reaches the builder and marks the build as modified.

# Environment files — contain the LiteLLM master key and OIDC client secret.
# Unlike git, docker matches a bare name at the root only, so **/ it is.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# SQLite databases — contain users' plaintext LiteLLM API keys
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# Build output
/keyosk
/server

# The instance `make seed` runs: its binary, database, log and manifest.
/dev/.seed/

# Traces the browser tests save when one fails.
/internal/browsertest/testdata/traces/

# OS / editor cruft
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp

# Browser-automation output, with the same exceptions as in .gitignore.
.playwright-mcp/
**/*.png
!web/static/apple-touch-icon.png
!docs/brand/*.png
!docs/content/images/screenshots/*.png

# Local tool settings and working files.
.claude/
docs/superpowers/

# The website's build output, cache, virtualenv and copied-in assets.
docs/site/
docs/.cache/
docs/.venv/
docs/content/assets/
